# 6a-ii — the reason-and-quantity view and the list. Sized `XL` and split in two
# 2026-09-27, on the day it was taken.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THIS IS THE FIRST SPLIT SINCE THE 2026-09-24 AMENDMENT WHOSE REASON IS PLAINLY
# SIZE, AND THE AGREEMENT ALLOWS IT FOR EXACTLY ONE LETTER: an `M` or an `L` is one
# sitting, `XL` still splits. The row carried `S/M, size it again` — an estimate made
# while it was still BLOCKED — and re-sizing it found `M` + `M`.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE CALIBRATION IS `5h-ii`, WHICH IS NOT AN ANALOGY BUT THE SAME WORK ON THE OTHER
# TWO KINDS. That row shipped the recent-documents list for `purchase` and `sale` and was
# split THREE ways: the list (`5h-ii-a`), the two controls (`5h-ii-b`), the note still in
# the queue (`5h-ii-c`). Waste's equivalent is those three PLUS a migration PLUS a pgTAP
# suite over a visibility claim. One row would be three of those children in a sitting.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ AND THE PARENT ROW ARGUED AGAINST THIS SPLIT IN WORDS, SO THE ARGUMENT IS ANSWERED
# RATHER THAN IGNORED: *"Corregir needs the lines and therefore needs the view, which is
# why the two are not split again — half an undo on the one screen with no history is a
# button that cancels something she cannot see."* That forbids shipping the CONTROLS
# without the view. It says nothing against shipping the view without the controls, which
# is exactly what `5h-ii-a` did and what the owner then judged on his phone. The order is
# held by `6a-ii-b`'s own gate cell and not by anybody's memory.
#
# ⚠️ THE TWO HALVES ALSO FAIL DIFFERENTLY, which is exception (2) arriving on top of the
# size: `6a-ii-a`'s failure class is A FENCE THAT LEAKS OR BLINDS — a definer view
# bypasses RLS on every table it touches, so the only instrument that can see it is a
# probe under `set role authenticated` and a contract check driving a real cashier over
# HTTP. `6a-ii-b`'s is THE LEDGER: a void writes a mirror document, and a correction that
# loses its race becomes a duplicate. Putting them in one row lets the fence nobody can
# look at ride in on the back of the list anybody can.
SPLIT_ID="6a-ii"
SPLIT_GROUPS=( "6a-ii|6a-ii-a 6a-ii-b" )
DELIVERABLES=(
  # ⚠️ ONE SPELLING PER ROW, never an alternation: a bare `|` in the regex field
  # truncates the entry and it fails downstream as a DROPPED deliverable, which reads
  # exactly like the defect this list exists to catch.
  #
  # ⚠️ NO BACKTICKS IN A REGEX — this file is SOURCED by bash. Match the words inside.
  #
  # ⚠️ EVERY REGEX MUST ALSO MATCH THE PARENT ROW; assertion 3 refuses a deliverable the
  # parent has stopped promising.
  "the reason-and-quantity view — 0041, the first definer view in this schema|0041|6a-ii-a"
  "DocumentKind gaining a third member, which @/api/documents was written to accept|DocumentKind|6a-ii-a"
  "waste in Lo último, which closes the gap 5h-ii-a named|Lo último|6a-ii-a"
  "Eliminar over void_transaction, which already works for a cashier today|Eliminar|6a-ii-b"
  "Corregir, which needs the lines and therefore needs the view|Corregir|6a-ii-b"
)
PHRASES=(
  "6a-ii-a|F|definer|The whole of the ruling, in one word. A security_invoker view over waste_line answered a cashier ZERO rows under set role authenticated on 2026-09-27 where a definer view stating its own predicate answered one — and all six views in this schema before 0041 were invoker — the database's count, relkind = 'v', never a grep of the migrations, so the shape is new and the sentence naming it is load-bearing."
  "6a-ii-a|I|writes nothing|5h-ii-a's argument, second time of asking, and the reason this child comes first. A list that only reads can be looked at on his phone and shipped before anything in this app has ever cancelled a write-off, and it is the surface the other child is reached from."
  "6a-ii-a|F|never|Bounds what the view carries. unit_cost_net_per_base is the column waste_line_select exists to fence, and a view that reaches around that policy and then selects it would hand a cashier the one number the owner did NOT trade away."
  "6a-ii-a|F|NO PESO FIGURE|Área 9's ruling of 2026-09-14 reaching a third screen. UNPRICED_WASTE sends a zero for a product with no shelf price, so waste.total_net is genuinely 0.00 for exactly the products most likely to spoil — and \$0.00 beside twenty kilos of tomatoes is what that ruling refuses."
  "6a-ii-b|F|LEDGER|The second failure class, and the reason this is its own row rather than a paragraph. void_transaction INSERTS a mirror document rather than editing one, so a correction that loses its race is a duplicate in the books — invisible on any screen, and nothing in 6a-ii-a can produce it."
  "6a-ii-b|F|5P-c|The re-pricing question this child inherits rather than discovers. waste_line stores the NET unit price and record_waste takes the GROSS, which is sale_line's mismatch exactly — so a corrected write-off is re-priced at today's shelf price, and that is a ruling the owner already owes on sales."
)
EACH_CHILD_SAYS=(
  # ⚠️ NOT `ships no migration` HERE — 6a-ii-a ships 0041 and the sentence would be false
  # of it, which is the same trap `6a.split`'s own comment records one level up.
  #
  # ⚠️⚠️ `measured` IS THE RIGHT SHARED STATEMENT BECAUSE EVERY DESIGN QUESTION IN BOTH
  # CHILDREN WAS ANSWERED BY A PROBE AND NOT BY READING: the invoker view's zero rows, the
  # two-key embed order, the nested embed that works and is refused anyway, and a
  # cashier's 200 on her own one-hour-old void. A child that names no measurement is a
  # child whose claims came from prose — which is the defect this repository has the most of.
  "I|measured|Both children were sized by driving a real PostgREST and a real Postgres rather than by reading migrations: 6a-ii-a's view shape, its line order and its denormalised product name each came off a probe, and 6a-ii-b's claim that Eliminar already works for a cashier is a 200 off the wire. A row that names no measurement is a row whose design came from prose."
)
